# Crypto Engine DISABLED — mainline sun8i-ce cannot drive the H713 CE (bench-
# proven 2026-07-23). Enabling it registers every algorithm, then each fails its
# known-answer self-test. Wiring the stock's 2nd interrupt (SPI 74) fixes task
# completion, but the CE then rejects mainline's task descriptors: ciphers report
# "address invalid", AES/SHA "algorithm not supported" — a different descriptor
# FORMAT (the vendor two-register-bank block), not an IRQ/clock/addressing gap.
# No CE TRNG either. Re-enabling needs descriptor-level RE of the vendor
# allwinner,sunxi-ce driver (source unavailable); the A53 has ARMv8 AES/SHA
# (software crypto ~2 GB/s, faster than this CE) so there is no benefit.
# See docs/status.md and docs/roadmap.md.
# CONFIG_CRYPTO_DEV_SUN8I_CE is not set
CONFIG_DMA_CMA=y
CONFIG_PRINTK_TIME=y
CONFIG_DYNAMIC_DEBUG=y
CONFIG_DEBUG_FS=y
# Reboot-to-fastboot handoff over the RTC GP7 nvmem cell (see the RTC section and
# the reboot-mode node in sun50i-h713.dtsi). Replaces the earlier syscon window
# that overlapped the RTC register region.
CONFIG_NVMEM_REBOOT_MODE=y
